	[PROSE]
		A meter is a **measurement**, not a progress bar: it shows where a value
		sits in a range that is known up front. For something that fills over
		time, reach for a progress bar instead.

		```svelte
		<Meter value={64} max={100} label="Docs coverage" />
		```
	[/PROSE]

	[COMPONENT component={Meter} status="experimental" args={{ value: 64, max: 100, label: 'Docs coverage' }}]
		<Meter {...args} />
	[/COMPONENT]

	[PROSE]
		### Reading a meter

		The fill is the value's share of the range, so a meter at half width is
		at half its maximum — not half done.
	[/PROSE]

	[EXAMPLE title="Full"]
		<Meter {...args} label="Shipped" value={100} />
	[/EXAMPLE]

